f1a-2-disclosure — empty-green check (§8.2)

THE QUESTION. `make disclosure` is green. Is it green because the
withholding in site/redact.py WORKS, or because the gate cannot turn red
on this repository's artifacts at all?

THE SWITCH. site/redact.py WITHHOLD_UNDECIDED, one line, off when
RABADON_PUBLISH_UNDECIDED=1 is set. Unset means WITHHOLD, so nothing in
CI rides on an environment variable being present.

date: 2026-08-26T02:48:16Z    commit: b688830

==============================================================
a. WITHHOLDING ON — the shipped default
==============================================================
$ python3 site/allowlist.py --list | tail -1
12 name(s) found, 12 allowed, 0 off-list
$ make disclosure
./native/published_allowlist_test.sh
published allowlist: a name is published by decision, not by default
  ok   - an off-list project name fails the check (exit 1)
  ok   - and the offending name is NAMED, so the human knows what to decide
  ok   - it reads the JSONL artifact too, not only the JSON one
  ok   - the allowed name is not reported — this is a decision gate, not a name census
  ok   - with every published name on the list the check passes (exit 0)
  ok   - comments, blank lines and surrounding space are not part of a name
  ok   - a missing allowlist allows NOTHING — it fails closed, not open
  ok   - an empty allowlist allows nothing either
  ok   - every project name published under site/ is on the allowlist

published allowlist: 9 ok, 0 fail
exit=0

