==============================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================
The green in (a) and (c) is bought by one rule: site/redact.py refuses to
publish a project name that is not on site/published-projects.txt. Turn
that rule off and the same two generators, reading the same ledger and the
same unredacted census, put 50 undecided names back under site/ and the
gate fails the build with exit 2. The check can turn red here, so its
green is a fact about the artifacts and not about the check.

50 in (b) against 41 before the work started: the ledger grew between the
two runs. The number is whatever the ledger says, and it is reported as
measured, not as it was quoted on the card.

NOT PROVEN BY THIS FILE. site/allowlist.py reads the `project` field a
record DECLARES; a name embedded in free text — a rule id, a detail
sentence, a quoted path — carries no such field, so neither the gate nor
this switch speaks for it. That class is still open. See the report.
